==Latin==

===Etymology===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*preyH-}}
Most likely for {{inh|la|itc-pro|*pro-}} + {{m|itc-pro|*prijos|t=own, dear}}, from {{der|la|ine-pro|*priHós|t=dear}}. Since ''pro-'' can hardly be explained as a nominal prefix, Forssman (2004) explains it as having been extended to the adjective from the verb {{m|la|priopriō|propriāre}}, [[hapax|once-attested]] as {{m|la|propriāssit}}. Cognate to {{cog|sa|प्रिय|tr=priyá|t=dear}}, {{cog|ru|прия́тель|t=buddy, mate}} and {{cog|ru|прия́тный|t=pleasant}}, {{cog|cy|rhydd|t=free}}, {{cog|en|free}}.

Other suggestions include:
* for {{m|la||*proprīvus}}, from the root of {{m|la|prīvus|t=individual}}, from {{der|la|ine-pro|*per-|*prey-wo-s|t=being in front}}.
* for {{m|la||*propatrius}}, from {{pre|la|pro-|pater|nocat=1}}, meaning “from one's forefathers”, taking {{cog|grc|προπάτωρ|t=forefather}} as comparison.

